{
  "name": "GitHub AI Coder - Advanced with Tools",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {},
      "id": "manual-trigger-adv",
      "name": "When clicking 'Test workflow'",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.manualTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [240, 400]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "assignments": {
          "assignments": [
            {
              "id": "feature_ticket",
              "name": "feature_ticket",
              "value": "={{ $json.feature_ticket || 'Add a new feature' }}",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "id": "repo_owner",
              "name": "repo_owner",
              "value": "={{ $json.repo_owner || 'username' }}",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "id": "repo_name",
              "name": "repo_name",
              "value": "={{ $json.repo_name || 'repository' }}",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "id": "base_branch",
              "name": "base_branch",
              "value": "={{ $json.base_branch || 'main' }}",
              "type": "string"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "set-input-adv",
      "name": "Input Parameters",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "typeVersion": 3.3,
      "position": [460, 400]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "authentication": "genericCredentialType",
        "genericAuthType": "httpHeaderAuth",
        "url": "=https://api.github.com/repos/{{ $json.repo_owner }}/{{ $json.repo_name }}",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "get-repo-adv",
      "name": "Get Repository Info",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [680, 400]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "authentication": "genericCredentialType",
        "genericAuthType": "httpHeaderAuth",
        "url": "=https://api.github.com/repos/{{ $json.repo_owner }}/{{ $json.repo_name }}/git/trees/{{ $('Get Repository Info').first().json.default_branch }}?recursive=1",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "get-tree-adv",
      "name": "Get File Structure",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [900, 400]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "authentication": "genericCredentialType",
        "genericAuthType": "httpHeaderAuth",
        "url": "=https://api.github.com/repos/{{ $('Input Parameters').first().json.repo_owner }}/{{ $('Input Parameters').first().json.repo_name }}/git/refs/heads/{{ $('Input Parameters').first().json.base_branch }}",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "get-sha-adv",
      "name": "Get Branch SHA",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [1120, 400]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// Prepare comprehensive context\nconst input = $('Input Parameters').first().json;\nconst repoInfo = $('Get Repository Info').first().json;\nconst treeInfo = $('Get File Structure').first().json;\nconst branchInfo = $('Get Branch SHA').first().json;\n\nconst branchName = `ai-agent/${input.feature_ticket.toLowerCase().replace(/[^a-z0-9]+/g, '-').substring(0, 50)}-${Date.now()}`;\n\n// Build file structure string\nconst fileStructure = (treeInfo.tree || [])\n  .filter(item => item.type === 'blob')\n  .map(item => item.path)\n  .slice(0, 100)\n  .join('\\n');\n\nreturn {\n  json: {\n    feature_ticket: input.feature_ticket,\n    repo_owner: input.repo_owner,\n    repo_name: input.repo_name,\n    base_branch: input.base_branch,\n    branch_name: branchName,\n    base_sha: branchInfo.object.sha,\n    repo_language: repoInfo.language || 'Unknown',\n    repo_description: repoInfo.description || '',\n    file_structure: fileStructure,\n    full_repo_name: `${input.repo_owner}/${input.repo_name}`\n  }\n};"
      },
      "id": "prep-context-adv",
      "name": "Prepare Context",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [1340, 400]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=You are an expert software engineer AI with access to GitHub repository tools.\n\n## Repository Context:\n- Repository: {{ $json.full_repo_name }}\n- Primary Language: {{ $json.repo_language }}\n- Description: {{ $json.repo_description }}\n- Base Branch: {{ $json.base_branch }}\n\n## Current File Structure:\n```\n{{ $json.file_structure }}\n```\n\n## Feature Request:\n{{ $json.feature_ticket }}\n\n## Available Tools:\nYou have access to these GitHub tools:\n1. **read_github_file**: Read existing files from the repository\n2. **search_github_code**: Search for code patterns in the repository\n3. **list_github_files**: List files in a directory\n\n## Your Task:\n1. Use the tools to understand the repository structure and existing code\n2. Read relevant existing files to understand patterns and conventions\n3. Generate production-ready code that integrates well with existing codebase\n4. Return ONLY a valid JSON object (no markdown) in this format:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"implementation_plan\": \"Detailed plan explaining your approach\",\n  \"files_read\": [\"list of files you read for context\"],\n  \"files\": [\n    {\n      \"path\": \"path/to/file.ext\",\n      \"content\": \"complete file content\",\n      \"action\": \"create or update\",\n      \"reason\": \"why this change is needed\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"pr_title\": \"feat: Concise title following conventional commits\",\n  \"pr_description\": \"## Summary\\n...\\n## Changes\\n...\\n## Testing\\n...\"\n}\n```\n\nGenerate the implementation now:",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "ai-agent-adv",
      "name": "AI Agent",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.agent",
      "typeVersion": 1.7,
      "position": [1560, 400]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "modelId": "claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022",
        "options": {
          "maxTokens": 8000,
          "temperature": 0.2
        }
      },
      "id": "claude-model-adv",
      "name": "Claude 3.5 Sonnet",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.lmChatAnthropic",
      "typeVersion": 1.7,
      "position": [1560, 600],
      "credentials": {
        "anthropicApi": {
          "id": "placeholder",
          "name": "Anthropic account"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "name": "read_github_file",
        "description": "Read a file from the GitHub repository. Provide the file path relative to repository root.",
        "workflowId": "={{ $workflow.id }}",
        "specifyInputSchema": true,
        "inputSchema": "{\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"file_path\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"Path to the file to read (e.g., 'src/index.js')\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\"file_path\"]\n}",
        "specifyOutputSchema": true,
        "outputSchema": "{\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"content\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"The file content\"\n    },\n    \"path\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  }\n}"
      },
      "id": "tool-read-file",
      "name": "Tool: Read GitHub File",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.toolWorkflow",
      "typeVersion": 1.1,
      "position": [1560, 800]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "name": "search_github_code",
        "description": "Search for code patterns in the repository. Useful for finding similar implementations or understanding conventions.",
        "workflowId": "={{ $workflow.id }}",
        "specifyInputSchema": true,
        "inputSchema": "{\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"query\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"Search query (e.g., 'function authentication' or 'import React')\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\"query\"]\n}",
        "specifyOutputSchema": true,
        "outputSchema": "{\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"results\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"object\"\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}"
      },
      "id": "tool-search-code",
      "name": "Tool: Search Code",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.toolWorkflow",
      "typeVersion": 1.1,
      "position": [1760, 800]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "name": "list_github_files",
        "description": "List files in a specific directory of the repository.",
        "workflowId": "={{ $workflow.id }}",
        "specifyInputSchema": true,
        "inputSchema": "{\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"directory_path\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"Directory path (e.g., 'src' or 'src/components'). Leave empty for root.\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": []\n}",
        "specifyOutputSchema": true,
        "outputSchema": "{\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"files\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}"
      },
      "id": "tool-list-files",
      "name": "Tool: List Files",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.toolWorkflow",
      "typeVersion": 1.1,
      "position": [1960, 800]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// Parse AI agent output\nconst agentOutput = $input.first().json;\nconst context = $('Prepare Context').first().json;\n\n// Extract response text\nlet responseText = agentOutput.output || agentOutput.text || JSON.stringify(agentOutput);\n\n// Clean up markdown code blocks if present\nif (responseText.includes('```')) {\n  responseText = responseText.replace(/```json\\n?/g, '').replace(/```/g, '').trim();\n}\n\n// Parse JSON\nconst parsed = JSON.parse(responseText);\n\nreturn {\n  json: {\n    ...context,\n    implementation_plan: parsed.implementation_plan,\n    files_read: parsed.files_read || [],\n    files: parsed.files || [],\n    pr_title: parsed.pr_title,\n    pr_description: parsed.pr_description\n  }\n};"
      },
      "id": "parse-adv",
      "name": "Parse AI Output",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [1780, 400]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "authentication": "genericCredentialType",
        "genericAuthType": "httpHeaderAuth",
        "method": "POST",
        "url": "=https://api.github.com/repos/{{ $json.repo_owner }}/{{ $json.repo_name }}/git/refs",
        "sendBody": true,
        "contentType": "json",
        "body": "={{ {\n  \"ref\": \"refs/heads/\" + $json.branch_name,\n  \"sha\": $json.base_sha\n} }}",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "create-branch-adv",
      "name": "Create Branch",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [2000, 400]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// Split files for individual commits\nconst data = $input.first().json;\nconst files = data.files || [];\n\nreturn files.map(file => ({\n  json: {\n    file_path: file.path,\n    file_content: file.content,\n    file_action: file.action || 'create',\n    file_reason: file.reason || '',\n    branch_name: data.branch_name,\n    repo_owner: data.repo_owner,\n    repo_name: data.repo_name,\n    pr_title: data.pr_title,\n    pr_description: data.pr_description,\n    base_branch: data.base_branch\n  }\n}));"
      },
      "id": "split-files-adv",
      "name": "Split Files",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [2220, 400]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "authentication": "genericCredentialType",
        "genericAuthType": "httpHeaderAuth",
        "method": "PUT",
        "url": "=https://api.github.com/repos/{{ $json.repo_owner }}/{{ $json.repo_name }}/contents/{{ $json.file_path }}",
        "sendBody": true,
        "contentType": "json",
        "body": "={{ {\n  \"message\": $json.file_action + \": \" + $json.file_path + \"\\n\\n\" + $json.file_reason,\n  \"content\": $base64Encode($json.file_content),\n  \"branch\": $json.branch_name\n} }}",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "commit-file-adv",
      "name": "Commit File",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [2440, 400]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "aggregate": "aggregateAllItemData",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "aggregate-adv",
      "name": "Aggregate Commits",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.aggregate",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [2660, 400]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "authentication": "genericCredentialType",
        "genericAuthType": "httpHeaderAuth",
        "method": "POST",
        "url": "=https://api.github.com/repos/{{ $json.repo_owner }}/{{ $json.repo_name }}/pulls",
        "sendBody": true,
        "contentType": "json",
        "body": "={{ {\n  \"title\": $json.pr_title,\n  \"body\": $json.pr_description + \"\\n\\n---\\n\\n🤖 **Auto-generated by AI Agent with GitHub Tools**\\n\\n**Files Analyzed:** \" + ($('Parse AI Output').first().json.files_read || []).join(', '),\n  \"head\": $json.branch_name,\n  \"base\": $json.base_branch\n} }}",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "create-pr-adv",
      "name": "Create Pull Request",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [2880, 400]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "assignments": {
          "assignments": [
            {
              "id": "pr_url",
              "name": "pr_url",
              "value": "={{ $json.html_url }}",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "id": "pr_number",
              "name": "pr_number",
              "value": "={{ $json.number }}",
              "type": "number"
            },
            {
              "id": "files_changed",
              "name": "files_changed",
              "value": "={{ $('Split Files').all().length }}",
              "type": "number"
            },
            {
              "id": "message",
              "name": "message",
              "value": "=✅ PR Created: {{ $json.html_url }}\\n📝 {{ $('Split Files').all().length }} files changed",
              "type": "string"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "output-adv",
      "name": "Success Output",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "typeVersion": 3.3,
      "position": [3100, 400]
    }
  ],
